Rock crabs are characterized by their robust, hard exoskeletons which provide protection against predators and harsh environments. They typically have a broad, flat body shape adapted to navigating rocky or sandy substrates.

#### 2. Color Patterns and Markings:
Rock crabs exhibit a variety of color patterns depending on their habitat. Common colors include shades of brown, green, and gray, often with mottled or speckled patterns that help them blend into their rocky or sandy surroundings. Some species may also display orange or red hues, particularly around the claws or legs.

