MLLM description: The Pekinese breed is characterized by its distinctive physical features, including a compact body, a short muzzle, and large, expressive eyes. Their fur is typically long and silky, often with a mix of colors such as black, brown, cream, or fawn, with some dogs having a bi-color coat. The coat can vary in length, with some dogs having a more profuse coat than others.

In terms of size and proportions, Pekinese are small dogs, usually weighing between 7-18 pounds and standing about 9-10 inches tall at the shoulder. They have a sturdy build with a slightly arched back and a short, square-shaped head.

Behaviorally, Pekinese are known to be affectionate, loyal, and sometimes stubborn. They can be quite vocal and may bark frequently. They are also prone to developing health issues related to their small size, such as respiratory problems and joint issues.

Unique identifying traits include their distinctive facial features, such as a flat face, large eyes, and a short muzzle. Their long, silky fur can also be a distinguishing feature, especially when it is well-groomed and styled. Overall, the Pekinese breed is easily recognizable due to these distinct physical characteristics and behavioral traits.
