MLLM description: The Keeshond breed is characterized by its distinctive physical features, including a thick, double-layered coat with a dense undercoat and a longer, coarser outer coat. This gives them a fluffy, lion-like appearance. Their color patterns can vary, but they typically have a gray or silver-gray base color with black markings on their face, ears, legs, and tail tip. They also have a white chest and paws.

In terms of size and proportions, Keeshonds are medium-sized dogs, generally standing between 18-20 inches tall at the shoulder and weighing around 35-45 pounds. They have a sturdy build with a broad head, expressive eyes, and a curled tail that often reaches above their back.

Behaviorally, Keeshonds are known to be intelligent, loyal, and affectionate. They are often described as having a "prince or princess" personality due to their regal appearance and confident demeanor. They are also highly energetic and require regular exercise and mental stimulation to stay happy and healthy.

Unique identifying traits include their distinctive facial markings, such as the black mask around their eyes and the black tip on their tail. Additionally, their thick, double-layered coat requires regular grooming to maintain its health and appearance.
