2. **Color Patterns and Markings**: Monarchs exhibit a striking orange and black coloration on their wings, with white spots along the edges. The veins of the wings are outlined in black, creating a bold contrast against the orange background. The underside of the wings is primarily yellow with black veins and white spots, providing camouflage when the butterfly is resting.

3. **Size and Proportions**: Monarch butterflies are medium-sized, with wingspan ranging from 2.8 to 3.6 inches (70–90 mm). Their body length is approximately 0.5 inches (13 mm).

