Broccoli is characterized by its compact, green flower heads composed of tightly clustered florets. These florets are surrounded by leafy green stems and leaves.

#### Color Patterns and Markings:
The primary color of broccoli is a vibrant green, with the florets appearing darker than the surrounding leaves. The leaves can have slight variations in shade depending on their age and exposure to sunlight.

#### Size and Proportions:
Broccoli typically has a round or slightly conical shape, with the flower head being the most prominent part. The size can vary, but it usually ranges from about 4 to 8 inches in diameter. The leaves extend outward from the base of the flower head.

#### Behavioral Characteristics:
Broccoli does not exhibit any behavioral characteristics as it is a plant and lacks the ability to move or respond to stimuli.

